---
import ClosingCTA from "../../components/ClosingCTA.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
import Video from "../../components/Video.astro";
import { guide, site } from "../../data/site";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const source = `${site.repo}/tree/52e5bc114e74ab8b8c3127f25463af53c7c36768/examples/demo`;
---

<BaseLayout
	description="Watch the SolidCraft enclosure demo: constrained sketch, shell, standoffs, cutouts, and a height change from 24 to 32 mm."
	title="A parametric Raspberry Pi enclosure · SolidCraft showcase"
>
	<section class="page-intro container">
		<p class="breadcrumb">
			<a href="/showcase/">Showcase</a>{" "}/ Parametric enclosure
		</p>
		<p class="eyebrow">PARAMETRIC MODELING / SOLIDCRAFT CONTRIBUTORS</p>
		<h1>Raspberry Pi enclosure.</h1>
		<p class="lead">
			Build a Raspberry Pi 4 enclosure with mounting posts, port cutouts, and
			vents, then change its height from 24 to 32 mm.
		</p>
	</section>
	<div class="container full-demo"><Video model="enclosure" /></div>
	<div class="container model-details">
		<div>
			<h2>How the enclosure is modeled.</h2>
			<p>
				The demonstration starts with a sketch dimensioned from board
				parameters, then extrudes, fillets, and shells it into an enclosure.
			</p>
			<p>
				An M2.5 standoff is patterned on the 58 × 49 mm mounting-hole rectangle.
				Port cutouts and vent slots follow, along with an engraved “Pi 4” label
				and a PETG material defined in the design.
			</p>
			<p>
				Finally, the height parameter changes from 24 to 32 mm, and the model
				rebuilds. The visible recording compresses the workflow to 6× playback
				with the pauses between actions removed.
			</p>
			<h2 style="margin-top:40px">Recording script and guides.</h2>
			<p>
				The source recording script and the maintained modeling guides describe
				how the example is created. Use them in your own environment and inspect
				the result before adapting it to a real part.
			</p>
			<a class="text-link" href={source}>
				Inspect the recording source<Icon name="external" size={18} />
			</a>
			<div class="notice">
				This is a modeling demonstration. No physical fit, manufacturing
				tolerance, or electrical suitability is asserted. The recording was made
				with SolidCraft 0.22.1, a build of the main branch, and is not a test of
				any release.
			</div>
		</div>
		<aside>
			<dl>
				<dt>Creator</dt>
				<dd>SolidCraft contributors</dd>
				<dt>Recording</dt>
				<dd>Recorded with SolidCraft 0.22.1 (its title bar shows v0.22.1)</dd>
				<dt>Playback</dt>
				<dd>6× · pauses removed · silent workflow recording</dd>
				<dt>License</dt>
				<dd>MIT OR Apache-2.0</dd>
				<dt>Source revision</dt>
				<dd><code>52e5bc114e74</code></dd>
			</dl>
			<a class="text-link" href={guide("parameters")}>
				Parameters guide<Icon name="external" size={18} />
			</a>
			<br>
			<a class="text-link" href={guide("features")} style="margin-top:16px">
				Solid features guide<Icon name="external" size={18} />
			</a>
		</aside>
	</div>
	<ClosingCTA />
</BaseLayout>
